**2. Purpose of the App**

We process information only to:

- create and manage your account  
- let you take or upload scan photos  
- generate wellness/educational scan reports  
- save reports and drafts on your device  
- manage subscriptions and scan limits  
- provide customer support  
- operate, secure, and improve the App  
- show ads on Android  
- send service notifications where enabled  

We do not use scan photos for advertising.

---

**3. Information we collect**

**3.1 Account information (required to create an account)**  
- Full name  
- Email address  
- Password (stored in protected/hashed form)  
- Email one-time passcode (OTP) used to verify your account or reset your password  

**3.2 Profile information (optional or user-provided)**  
- Profile photo, if you upload one  
- Display name for a scan, if you enter one  

**3.3 Scan and wellness information**  
When you start a scan and tap **Allow**, we process:  
- Front-facing scan photo  
- Side-profile scan photo  
- Age  
- Gender  
- Optional name, if you entered one  
- The wellness report generated from that scan  

On-device Google ML Kit Face Detection is used only to help you frame the photo. Live camera frames from that helper are not stored and are not sent to Gemini.

The App does not collect Face ID, TrueDepth, 3D face maps, or biometric templates for identity or device unlock. Scan photos are 2D photographs.

**3.4 Subscription and purchase information**  
If you buy a plan: product/plan identifiers, purchase or entitlement status, and scan-limit / subscription status. Payments are processed by Apple App Store or Google Play. We do not receive your full payment-card number.

**3.5 Device and technical information**  
App version, diagnostics, identifiers used by analytics and (on Android) advertising SDKs, push-notification token if notifications are used, language/locale, and technical logs created when you connect to our servers.

**3.6 Advertising information (Android only)**  
Google AdMob may collect advertising identifiers, app activity, device identifiers, and diagnostics to show ads. Ads are not enabled on iOS in the current App.

**3.7 Support communications**  
If you email us, we receive that message and the email address you use.

